# The same choice through an opaque formal (RECEPTION-EDGE-DEBTS (d)): run's p holds a Model in one call and a Thin
# in the other.  get(p) admits the Model, 4; the Thin is refused where run forms the input and run's handler takes
# it, 42.  Until 2026-10-05 this program met the internal error of OPAQUE-ACTUAL-KNOWN-LAYOUT, "a pair map of D-105
# was asked for after the maps were declared".  Entry 7.
Model:
    size_t: value 4U
end: Model

Thin:
    int: pad 1
end: Thin

good: merge: Model
bad: merge: Thin

fn: get (Model: x) size_t
return: x\value

fn: run (@: void p) size_t
    size_t: r 0U
    r: get(p)
    catch: implements ()
        r: 42U
    ---
return: r

size_t: a run(good)
size_t: b run(bad)
int: ok 7
if: a != 4U
    ok: 81
if: b != 42U
    ok: 82
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
